<%# THE EXITS LAB, FRONT DOOR: the vantages already typed, the counter-figure
    over all of them, and the form for one more. `Lab::Exits`'s header is the
    design and the captain's answers in his own words.

    THE COUNTER-FIGURE AND THE REFUSAL ARE HERE AND NOWHERE ELSE, which is the
    captain's Call 5 of 2026-09-08 and `Lab::Exits::Alignment`'s header: both are
    properties of the SET of vantages, and a per-vantage reading of either would
    invite reading one place's open country as the game's.

    THE FORM IS SIX FACTS AND NOT ONE PROMPT FIELD. See `Lab::Exits`'s header for
    why a prompt box here would be a second prompt source with no baseline. %>
<%= render "lab/styles" %>
<%= render "lab/exits/styles" %>

<h1>the exits lab</h1>
<p class="nav">
  <%= link_to "&larr; the stories".html_safe, root_path %>
  &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; <%= link_to "the realization lab", lab_kinds_path %>
  &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; what the model says lies beyond a place you type, on a copy
  of a world that is rolled back afterwards
  &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; <span class="warn">drawing a sample spends money</span>
</p>

<h2>over every vantage</h2>
<% reach = @alignment.reach %>
<div class="panel">
  <p class="note">
    The two figures the rates are checked against, and neither is one you can
    pass. A band handed to a place the world already held is discarded by
    <code>Location::Generator#connect_exit!</code>, so the gap between them is
    the share of picks that decided nothing.
  </p>
  <% if reach.judgeable? %>
    <div class="fields">
      <div class="k">insides given</div>
      <div class="v">
        <%= reach.given %> of <%= reach.named %> places named
        <span class="absent">(<%= number_to_percentage(reach.given_share * 100, precision: 1) %>)</span>
      </div>
      <div class="k">insides reaching</div>
      <div class="v">
        <span class="<%= reach.reaching.positive? ? "pick hit" : "pick miss" %>">
          <%= reach.reaching %> of <%= reach.named %>
        </span>
        <span class="absent">(<%= number_to_percentage(reach.reaching_share * 100, precision: 1) %>)</span>
        &mdash; the ones the engine actually opened
      </div>
      <div class="k">discarded</div>
      <div class="v">
        <%= reach.discarded %>
        <span class="absent">
          (a band on a place that already existed. A vantage with many of these
          wants more names in its <code>absent</code> list)
        </span>
      </div>
    </div>
  <% else %>
    <p class="absent">(nothing drawn yet, so there is nothing to check anything against)</p>
  <% end %>
</div>

<h2>alignment</h2>
<% figure = @alignment.figure %>
<div class="panel">
  <% if figure.nil? %>
    <p class="warn"><%= @alignment.refusal %></p>
    <p class="note">
      This is a refusal and not a missing feature. The exits prompt's own first
      instruction on the field is <em>&ldquo;say NO INSIDE for almost all of
      them&rdquo;</em>, so a set of nothing but <code>none of them</code> vantages
      reads full marks for a model that has emptied the game of buildings &mdash;
      which is a prompt version this project has already shipped and measured.
      <code>Lab::Exits::Alignment</code>'s header has the argument.
    </p>
  <% else %>
    <p>
      <span class="<%= figure.established? ? "pick hit" : "pick unscored" %>">
        <%= figure.fraction %>
      </span>
      draws satisfied their own quantifier<%= " -- not established" unless figure.established? %>
    </p>
    <p class="note">
      Pooled over draws and not averaged over vantages, because a vantage drawn
      thirty times and one drawn twice are not two equal opinions. Shapes held:
      <%= figure.allowed %>.
    </p>
  <% end %>
</div>

<h2>the vantages</h2>
<% if @vantages.empty? %>
  <p class="absent">(none yet &mdash; type one below)</p>
<% else %>
  <div class="scroll">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>vantage</th><th>world</th><th>off the books</th><th>expects</th>
          <th>drawn</th><th>answers</th><th>judged</th><th>reaching</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <% @vantages.each do |vantage| %>
          <% rate = vantage.hit_rate %>
          <tr>
            <td><%= link_to vantage.name, lab_exits_vantage_path(vantage) %></td>
            <td><%= vantage.world %></td>
            <td>
              <% if vantage.absent_names.empty? %>
                <span class="warn">nothing</span>
              <% else %>
                <%= vantage.absent_names.size %>
              <% end %>
            </td>
            <td><%= debug_value(vantage.expects_inside_quantifier, absent: "nothing") %></td>
            <td><%= rate.drawn %></td>
            <%# HOW MANY DIFFERENT ANSWERS, beside how many draws -- the one
                figure on this page that is advice rather than a score. See
                `HitRate#distinct_answers`. %>
            <td><%= rate.distinct_answers %> distinct</td>
            <td><%= rate.judged %></td>
            <td>
              <% if rate.reach.judgeable? %>
                <%= rate.reach.reaching %> of <%= rate.reach.named %>
              <% else %>
                <span class="absent">&mdash;</span>
              <% end %>
            </td>
          </tr>
        <% end %>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
<% end %>

<h2>a new vantage</h2>
<%= render "lab/exits/vantages/form", vantage: @vantage %>
